10. Malware Scanning vs Hash Reputation Analysis
This is an important exam distinction.
Hash Reputation Analysis
Checks the file’s hash against known malicious hashes.
File
 ↓
Hash
 ↓
Known Malware Hash Database
 ↓
Match?
Example:
File Hash = ABC123

Known:
ABC123 = Malware

       ↓

Detection
Limitation
A new or modified malware sample may have a hash that is not yet known.
 
⸻
 
Malware Scanning
Performs a deeper inspection of the file’s contents using Microsoft Defender Antivirus.
File
 ↓
Content Inspection
 ↓
Malware Detection
 ↓
Result
Comparison
Feature	Hash Reputation	Malware Scanning
Checks file hash	✅	✅ Can use reputation information
Inspects file contents	Limited	✅
Can detect unknown/modified threats	More limited	Broader detection capability
Depth of inspection	Lower	Higher
Exam memory	Hash lookup	Full malware inspection
Easy Memory: Hash Reputation = “Check the ID.” Malware Scanning = “Inspect the file.”
Malware Scanning is available as part of the new Defender for Storage plan and is a separately charged capability.
 
