Exam & Interview Questions
What is Microsoft Defender for Storage?
A Microsoft Defender for Cloud service that protects Azure Storage from threats such as malicious uploads, suspicious access, data exfiltration, and other security risks.
Is Defender for Storage agent-based?
No. It is an agentless cloud security service.
What are the three main capabilities to remember?
Activity Monitoring, Malware Scanning, and Sensitive Data Threat Detection.
What powers Malware Scanning?
Microsoft Defender Antivirus (MDAV).
What is the difference between Malware Scanning and Hash Reputation Analysis?
Hash Reputation Analysis compares a file’s hash with known malicious hashes, while Malware Scanning performs deeper inspection of supported file contents.
What is data exfiltration?
Unauthorized or suspicious removal of data from an environment, such as downloading large amounts of data from a storage account.
Why is sensitive-data detection useful?
It provides additional context about the importance of the data involved in suspicious activity.
Can Defender detect suspicious SAS token usage?
It can identify suspicious storage access patterns, including activity associated with SAS-based access.
What storage services should you remember for the exam?
Blob Storage, Azure Files, and Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2, with specific advanced capabilities varying by storage type.
Does Defender for Storage require diagnostic agents to be installed?
No. It is an agentless managed service.
 
